            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56753804?u=0f698c1d89d7bc8d64ee9c423a5549147a91b866&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Clarifies in the Performance API documentation that canceled HTTP requests are still recorded as performance entries, but their <code class=\"notranslate\">requestStart</code> timestamp will be 0. This update helps developers avoid calculation errors when analyzing performance metrics for canceled requests.</p>",
